        "biblical_teaching": "The retrieved passages complicate an absolute 'zero scriptures' claim. Judges 4:4 identifies Deborah as \"a prophetess\" who \"judged Israel,\" a position of national leadership, and Acts 21:9 records that Philip \"had four virgin daughters who prophesied.\" 1 Corinthians 11:5 assumes women pray and prophesy in the gathered assembly — \"every woman praying or prophesying with her head uncovered dishonors her head\" — regulating the manner of the practice rather than forbidding it outright.",
