        "biblical_teaching": "Jesus warns that \"not everyone who says to me, 'Lord, Lord,' will enter into the Kingdom of Heaven; but he who does the will of my Father who is in heaven\" (Matthew 7:21). James teaches that \"faith, if it has no works, is dead in itself\" (James 2:17) and repeats that \"faith apart from works is dead\" (James 2:26), insisting that genuine faith is demonstrated rather than merely professed (James 2:18). Together these passages support that authentic Christian identity involves more than a single verbal or ritual act.",
