        "biblical_teaching": "Luke 9:23, as retrieved, reads: \"If anyone desires to come after me, let him deny himself, take up his cross, and follow me\" — a call to self-denial and cross-bearing as the mark of discipleship. The same core teaching appears in Matthew 16:24 and Mark 8:34, and is reinforced by Matthew 10:38 (\"he who doesn't take his cross and follow after me isn't worthy of me\"), showing this is a repeated, central description of what it means to follow Jesus rather than an isolated saying.",
