        "broader_teaching": "The contrast between spiritual burden and Christian freedom or rest has deep roots across the tradition: Augustine's restless heart, the Reformation's emphasis on grace versus the burden of self-justification, and broader Christian teaching on the crushing yoke of legalism versus the easy yoke of Christ are all variations on this theme. Traditions vary in emphasis, but agree that following Christ is meant to relieve rather than add spiritual weight.",
