        "biblical_teaching": "The retrieved passages don't directly verify the historical claim that the early post-apostolic church accurately preserved Jesus's teaching. What they do show is a New Testament ethic of enduring faithfulness: believers are told to guard the deposit of faith entrusted to them (2 Timothy 1:14), to 'be faithful to death' for a martyr's crown of life (Revelation 2:10; James 1:12), and are pictured overcoming 'because of the Lamb's blood, and because of the word of their testimony,' not loving their lives even to death (Revelation 12:11). These describe a called-for character within the apostolic era itself, not a documented record of whether the sub-apostolic church actually transmitted doctrine without distortion.",
