        "broader_teaching": "Retaining religious form while denying its substance is a recurring theme in Christian tradition's treatment of heresy and nominal faith, from patristic anti-Gnostic polemics through Reformation-era warnings about dead orthodoxy to modern evangelical and Catholic critiques of syncretistic reinterpretations of Christian vocabulary. Traditions differ on which specific modern movements qualify and how charitably to characterize their intent, as deliberate deception versus sincere reinterpretation, which is a matter of pastoral judgment rather than settled doctrine.",
