        "confidence": "high",
        "biblical_teaching": "Proverbs 14:1 states almost word-for-word what the speaker says: 'Every wise woman builds her house, but the foolish one tears it down with her own hands.' The surrounding wisdom tradition reinforces the same builder and destroyer contrast: Proverbs 9:1 pictures Wisdom herself building 'her house,' Proverbs 24:3 states 'Through wisdom a house is built,' and Proverbs 11:29 warns that 'He who troubles his own house shall inherit the wind,' together treating wisdom and folly as decisive, house-shaping forces.",
        "broader_teaching": "This proverb is read across Christian and Jewish wisdom tradition as commending practical household wisdom broadly; the underlying term for 'house' carries the sense of household or family line, not merely a physical structure. Since the wisdom-versus-folly contrast is applied elsewhere to sons, kings, and communities as well, most interpreters read this as one instance of a larger biblical framework about wisdom and folly's consequences, applied here to household management, rather than a claim uniquely essentializing women's moral nature.",
        "speaker_alignment": "The speaker's quotation is an accurate, near-verbatim rendering of the proverb; saying 'home' for 'house' and dropping the word 'Every' doesn't change its meaning or claim. His application, that wives hold real power to build up or tear down the household more than they may realize, is a direct and faithful application of the verse's own claim rather than an imposition on it.",
