        "biblical_teaching": "Genesis narrates that the serpent approached and deceived the woman directly (Genesis 3:4, 13), and 1 Timothy 2:14 confirms that Eve specifically was the one deceived by the serpent's craftiness. None of the retrieved passages state that the serpent targeted Eve because Adam was passive or \"did not activate,\" or that Satan then \"became head of household\" -- the text simply records that the serpent spoke to the woman, without explaining why her rather than Adam.",
